"settings.fastAvifQuality" = "Fixed quality (Q)";
"settings.fastAvifQuality.help" = "Enter Q from 10 to 100; progressive AVIF requires at least Q10. Higher Q means higher quality, but no value universally guarantees lossless RGB. Archive rules may accept a true-lossless result first. Q affects only new lossy encodes; existing AVIF files are not re-encoded.";
"settings.fastAvifSpeed" = "Encoding speed (Speed)";
"settings.fastAvifSpeed.help" = "Enter Speed from 0 (slowest) to 10 (fastest). This is not compression effort (E). Archive rules may accept a true-lossless result first. Speed affects new true-lossless probes and lossy encodes; Q affects only new lossy encodes. Existing AVIF files are not re-encoded.";
"settings.imgJxlSearch.help" = "Try the selected level and a few lower preset levels, keeping verified smaller image data; this can take longer. E sets encoding work, not image quality D. When D is also automatic, select E first, then search D. Reversible JPEG transcoding is configured separately.";
"settings.imgJpegSearch.help" = "By default, compare E1–E11 independently and keep the smallest verified JXL; this takes more time. If any level cannot complete, record a failure and retain the source. Partial comparison tests only selected preset levels; manual fixed uses one level. All preserve exact JPEG reconstruction and do not use pixel quality D.";
"settings.imgQualitySearch.help" = "Only applies to sources the archive rules already allow to be lossy; PNG stays lossless and JPEG reconstruction stays reversible. Explicit D search keeps but does not use the manual value and starts from a lossless D0 baseline. Archive-rule mode searches only when its existing conditions call for it; otherwise it uses the manual value or rule baseline.";
